// What is about panics (spec 06-syntax.md §6.1, 01-safety.md §1.3): `panic(message)`, which the
// compiler declares here and `std` re-exports, and the checks built-in arrays make, for a container
// whose index isn't its storage's, such as a ring buffer on an `Array`. Each reports its caller's
// location, as the built-in checks do.

// Panics unless 0 <= index < length.
@CallerLocation
pub extern void checkIndex(int index, int length);

// Panics unless the `count` elements from `start` are within a sequence of `length`.
@CallerLocation
pub extern void checkRange(int start, int count, int length);
